# FileCommander

Touch file manager for the board's local storage. On Pico the local provider is
littlefs on the reserved internal flash region; on Linux it is the configured
local directory. The user can navigate, create empty files and folders,
rename, delete with confirmation, view files as text or hex, and inspect
volume information. On Pico, a confirmed erase action wipes the reserved flash
region, formats it as LittleFS, and mounts the new volume.
The volume selector also mounts the board's FAT-formatted SD card at `/sd`.
